  "solution": "**Given:**\n\ny - (1/y) = 4\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nIf y - (1/y) = P then,\n\ny + (1/y) = √(P2 + 4)\n\nIf y + (1/y) = P then,\n\ny³ + (1/y³) = P³ - 3P\n\n**Calculation:**\n\ny - (1/y) = 4\n\n⇒ y + (1/y) = √(42 + 4) = √20\n\n⇒ y + (1/y) = 2√5\n\nNow,\n\ny3 + (1/y3) = (2√5)3 - 3 × 2√5\n\n⇒ 40√5 - 6√5 = 34√5\n\ny3 + (1/y3) = 34√5\n\nSquaring both sides\n\n⇒ {y3 + (1/y3)}² = (34√5)²\n\n⇒ y⁶ + (1/y⁶) + 2 = 1156 × 5\n\n⇒ y6 + (1/y6) = (5780 - 2) = 5778\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 5778. **",
